35 years ago the hiv  pandemic made international headlines  for the first time  since then 78 million people have become  infected with  hiv and 35 million have died from  aids-related illnesses world aids day is  an important reminder for  us all that hiv aids has not gone away  for the eu combating hiv aids remains a  priority  under horizon 2020 the commission is  continuing to support research  to develop novel or improved tools  against  hiv by april 2020 the commission  had already committed over 220 million  euros with the covet 19 pandemic  disproportionately affecting  vulnerable groups we must step up our  efforts  in raising awareness of the impact of  hiv  on people's lives and on leaving no one  behind  particularly those who are marginalized  or live in rural areas  we must act to end the widespread  discrimination and stigma  against people with or thought to have  hiv aids  the world aids day is a call for us to  renew our long-term  commitments and to commit to finding  innovative solutions  together we will build a culture of  solidarity  trust and perseverance
 

